class.description:
[ResourceLocalizationServer] is the resource server of the localization system. It replaces the project setting [code]internationalization/locale/translation_remaps[/code] (the Remaps tab of the Localization settings), which is [b]deprecated[/b] for game code. It reads [ResourceLocalizationCatalog]s; their keys are the original resource paths (see [LocalizationServer] for layers, priorities and the locale chain).
[b]load() follows the locale:[/b] [method @GDScript.load], [method ResourceLoader.load], [code]preload()[/code]ed scenes and threaded loading load the localized file of the active locale and cache it under the original path. Nothing has to change in scenes or scripts.
[b]Which path is used:[/b] for each original path, the locale with the best match to the active locale ([method TranslationServer.compare_locales]: [code]de_DE[/code] takes [code]de_DE[/code], then [code]de[/code], then another country such as [code]de_AT[/code]), then the fallback locale. When two layers match equally, the higher priority wins. This gives the same results as [code]translation_remaps[/code]. If the localized file does not exist, the original is loaded with a warning.
[b]Locale changes without a hitch:[/b] after a locale or catalog change, every cached resource whose localized path changed is loaded again on worker threads and updated in place, like [constant ResourceLoader.CACHE_MODE_REPLACE]: nodes that use it show the new data, their [signal Resource.changed] signals come on the main thread. When all are done, [signal resources_relocalized] is emitted. Without worker threads (single-threaded Web export), the resources are loaded during the locale change, as before.
[b]Old remaps and mods:[/b] [method LocalizationServer.load_project_catalogs] imports [code]translation_remaps[/code] as the first layer of priority 0, then adds [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/localization/resource_catalogs] and, with a higher priority, [member ProjectSettings.internationalization/localization/resource_external_catalogs] (for example [code]user://mods/*/voice/*.lcat[/code]). Mods can also be added with [method LocalizationServer.add_catalog_list].
[b]Editor:[/b] like [code]translation_remaps[/code], [method @GDScript.load] in the editor loads the original resources, so scenes are edited with them. The methods of this class work in the editor too.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
# The catalog lists the German and Polish voice line of res://voice/intro.ogg.
var catalog = ResourceLocalizationCatalog.new()
catalog.set_localized_path(&"res://voice/intro.ogg", "de", "res://voice/de/intro.ogg")
ResourceLocalizationServer.add_catalog(catalog)

LocalizationServer.set_locale("de")
$Voice.stream = load("res://voice/intro.ogg") # Loads res://voice/de/intro.ogg.
print(ResourceLocalizationServer.get_localized_path("res://voice/intro.ogg", "fr")) # res://voice/intro.ogg

# Wait until cached resources follow a locale change.
LocalizationServer.set_locale("en")
await ResourceLocalizationServer.resources_relocalized
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
// The catalog lists the German voice line of res://voice/intro.ogg.
var catalog = new ResourceLocalizationCatalog();
catalog.SetLocalizedPath("res://voice/intro.ogg", "de", "res://voice/de/intro.ogg");
// Inherited methods and signals are reached through the singleton instance.
ResourceLocalizationServer.Singleton.AddCatalog(catalog);

LocalizationServer.SetLocale("de");
GetNode<AudioStreamPlayer>("Voice").Stream = GD.Load<AudioStream>("res://voice/intro.ogg");
GD.Print(ResourceLocalizationServer.GetLocalizedPath("res://voice/intro.ogg", "fr"));

LocalizationServer.SetLocale("en");
await ToSignal(ResourceLocalizationServer.Singleton, "resources_relocalized");
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
